# Local trace stores. Pruned from the leak-guard walk in
# tests/test_public_hygiene.py, so they must not be committable: this is a
# PUBLIC repo and that guard exists to stop internal references from shipping.
# Ignoring them is what makes pruning them safe -- otherwise a `git add -A`
# could commit local trace data into a directory the scanner is told to skip.
.scholia/
.scholialang/

# The two internal RSI/operator scratch dirs are also pruned from that walk,
# but are deliberately NOT named here: spelling an internal codename in a
# public .gitignore is itself the leak the guard blocks. Ignore them locally
# with `.git/info/exclude`, which is never published.
